    "final_answer": "An unintentionally foaming cement slurry appears light in the surface densitometer. [KB4]\nThis reading may underestimate downhole density because the entrapped air in the foam compresses under pressure, making the actual density greater than the surface measurement. [KB4]\nSevere foaming can threaten hydrostatic pressure during pumping because it can cause cavitation in the pumps, leading to loss of hydrostatic pressure. [KB4]",
